# Color (reasonable delta table)
#
# Packet 1's skip count has been carefully chosen as $10
# so that during testing (assuming no bugs) the first 16
# colors in the VERA palette will not be affected.  This
# saves us from the colors going wonky during testing,
# and it also tests the skip functionality.

          # DWORD size (already streamed)
          #  WORD type (already streamed)
0200      #  WORD number of packets

          # Packet 0
02        #  BYTE skip count
01        #  BYTE copy count
3A2B1C    #       r,g,b for first color

          # Packet 1
01        #  BYTE skip count
02        #  BYTE copy count
191919    #       r,g,b for first color
2C2C2C    #       r,g,b for second color

# We expect different VERA RGB values for 64 and 256 color.
# In both cases, the most significant 4 bits of RGB color are used.
#
# 3A2B1C is 00111010 00101011 00011100
#  6-bit is   1110     1010     0111   -> VERA A70E
#  8-bit is 0011     0010     0001     -> VERA 2103
#
# 191919 is 00011001 00011001 00011001
#  6-bit is   0110     0110     0110   -> VERA 6606
#  8-bit is 0001     0001     0001     -> VERA 1101
#
# 2C2C2C is 00101100 00101100 00101100
#  6-bit is   1011     1011     1011   -> VERA BB0B
#  8-bit is 0010     0010     0010     -> VERA 2202



    
